  "body": "The non-standard `-webkit-text-security` property exists in both webkit and blink, but does not seem to be mentioned in the compatibility standard.\r\n\r\nWe've seen real-world webcompat issues because this property is not implemented in Firefox; see https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1826629 and https://github.com/webcompat/web-bugs/issues/114591.\r\n\r\n(There's some information about `-webkit-text-security` [on MDN](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/-webkit-text-security), but note that it is not entirely complete or accurate at present.)\r\n\r\nNote also that `-webkit-text-security` is entirely distinct from the ([questionable](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/6788)) CSS-UI-4 `input-security` property.\r\n",
